{"study_accession":"PRJNA1074332","secondary_study_accession":"SRP488757","title":"The SUMOylation inhibitor TAK-981 induces a transcriptional reprogramming in human Natural Killer cells [RNA-seq]","description":"SUMOylation, a post-translational modification of the ubiquitin family plays a critical role in the regulation of proteins function and fate. TAK-981 (Subasumstat) is a first-in-class inhibitor of the SUMO-activating enzyme used in various phase I/II clinical trials for solid tumors and lymphomas. In addition to its direct cytotoxic effect on cancer cells, TAK-981 activates anti-tumor immune response. We show here that TAK-981 activates human natural killer cells. TAK-981 mostly regulates genes involved in inflammation and immune response, in particular those related to the type-I and type-II interferon pathway. Overall design: Total RNA was purified from FACS-sorted NK cells (CD56+/CD3-) sorted from 3 different healthy donors' blood treated with mock or 100 nM TAK-981 for 24 h.","pubmed":"40661051","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN39859515","study_accession":"PRJNA1074332","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"NK_TAK981_rep3 (RNA-seq)","description":"NK_TAK981_rep3 (RNA-seq)","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8068098","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-03-24","attributes":[["source_name","blood"],["tissue","blood"],["cell_type","natural killer"],["treatment","TAK_981"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR27906795","experiment_accession":"SRX23566771","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":57175338,"base_count":5717533800,"first_public":"2024-03-24","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8068098: NK_TAK981_rep3 (RNA-seq) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN39859516","study_accession":"PRJNA1074332","blood_c